---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import PhotoCarousel from '../components/PhotoCarousel.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { href, site } from '../data/site';
const personalPhotos = [
  {key:'alps-view',alt:'A hiker on a rocky ridge above cloud-filled valleys in the Alps.',caption:'Hiking above the clouds in the Alps.'},
  {key:'alps-1',alt:'Elias wearing a backpack on a mountain trail in the Alps.',caption:'Backpacking in the Alps.'},
  {key:'alps-2',alt:'A hiker crossing rocky terrain below a steep mountain ridge.',caption:'Crossing rocky terrain in the Alps.'},
  {key:'squamish-1',alt:'Elias climbing a granite face on a rope in Squamish.',caption:'Rock climbing in Squamish, British Columbia.'},
  {key:'squamish-2',alt:'A top-down view of Elias climbing a granite wall on a red rope.',caption:'Another route in Squamish.'},
  {key:'rockies',alt:'Elias looking over a mountain valley in the Rockies.',caption:'Hiking in the Canadian Rockies.'},
  {key:'nepal',alt:'A Nepal trekking route lined with colourful prayer flags.',caption:'Our 2023 Everest Base Camp trek and Youth Haven fundraiser.'},
  {key:'biking',alt:'Elias mountain biking on a forest trail.',caption:'Mountain biking.'},
  {key:'guitar',alt:'Close-up of a hand playing an acoustic guitar.',caption:'Playing guitar.'}
];
const timeline = [
  {year:'HIGH SCHOOL',title:'Learning by building—and teaching',text:'Personal electronics projects, a VEX robot, and an after-school VEX IQ club for 8–11 elementary students each year in Grades 11 and 12.'},
  {year:'2024',title:'Student captain, FRC Team 9580',text:'A rookie season of mechanical design, fabrication, electrical work and learning how a team brings a robot together.'},
  {year:'2024–25',title:'From student to mentor',text:'At Western, I became a general mentor for Team 4617, teaching mechanical skills and helping with the Reefscape elevator.'},
  {year:'2025–NOW',title:'WE FIRST president & FRC lead mentor',text:'Supporting student projects, workshops and Team 4617, alongside team administration and faculty support.'},
  {year:'SUMMER 2026',title:'Production engineering at FIO',text:'Root-cause analysis, equipment upgrades, prototype iteration and installation coordination in automotive manufacturing.'}
];
---
<Layout title="About Me" active="about" description="Meet Elias Coleshill: a dual-degree engineering student, robotics builder and mentor who loves the outdoors." image="media/ski-1400.webp">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="about-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">ABOUT ME</span><h1>Hi, I’m Elias<span>.</span></h1><p class="about-lead">I like having an idea for something I need, then working through the design until I can build it.</p><p>I’m in my third year at Western University, studying <strong>Mechatronics Systems Engineering</strong> and <strong>Artificial Intelligence Systems Engineering</strong> together in a five-year dual-degree program. I expect to graduate in 2029.</p><p>Robotics gives me a chance to work on the mechanisms, electronics and code in the same project. I enjoy figuring out why something isn’t behaving the way I expected, changing the design and testing it again. A lot of my favourite projects started because I wanted to try an idea for myself.</p><p>I’m looking for a four-month co-op from <strong>May to August 2027</strong>. Robotics, product development, embedded controls and mechanical design all interest me. I’d love to work on things like 3D printers, satellites or mobile robots, and I’m open to other industries where I can help develop and build a product.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Get in touch<Icon name="external" size={17}/></a><a class="button" href={href('files/Elias_Coleshill_Resume.pdf')} target="_blank" rel="noopener">My résumé<Icon name="download" size={17}/></a></div></div><figure><Photo image="ski" alt="Elias outdoors in ski gear on a snowy mountain." eager class="about-main-photo"/><figcaption class="photo-caption">Skiing is one of my favourite ways to spend time outdoors.</figcaption></figure></section>
    <section class="about-details"><div><span class="eyebrow">ROBOTICS & TEACHING</span><h2>Running WE FIRST<br/>and mentoring Team Dawn</h2><p>I’ve been teaching robotics since high school, starting with an after-school VEX IQ club for elementary students. At Western, I became involved in WE FIRST and FRC Team 4617, Team Dawn. I now run the club and serve as the team’s lead mentor with faculty support.</p><p>I like helping people learn how to research a part, read a datasheet or debug a mechanism. The goal is to give them enough understanding to develop their own design, especially when the next problem looks different from the example we worked through.</p><p>I’m also affiliated with Western’s Sunstangs solar car team.</p><a class="text-link" href={href('projects/robotics-teaching/')} style="margin-top:24px">Robotics teaching and leadership<Icon name="external" size={17}/></a></div><div class="timeline">{timeline.map(item => <div class="timeline-item"><span class="mono">{item.year}</span><div><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p></div></div>)}</div></section>
    <section class="about-award"><Photo image="award" alt="Elias receiving the Lady Godiva Award at the engineering formal."/><div><span class="eyebrow">LADY GODIVA AWARD / 2026</span><h2>Robotics teaching and community service</h2><p>I received the Lady Godiva Award in the winter term of second year. It recognizes self-sacrifice and devotion to the Western Engineering community, and I received it for my commitment to WE FIRST, the university robotics workshops and FRC mentoring.</p><p>I spend a lot of time on those teams because I enjoy seeing students become comfortable enough with the tools and ideas to take a project in their own direction.</p></div></section>
    <section class="outdoor-gallery"><span class="eyebrow">OUTSIDE ENGINEERING</span><h2>Skiing, climbing, hiking and music</h2><p>I love spending time outdoors, whether that’s on skis, a mountain bike, a climbing route or a long hike. The photos below include backpacking in the Alps, climbing in Squamish and trips in the Rockies. I also play guitar.</p><p>In 2023, my family and I trekked to Everest Base Camp and used the trip to raise funds for Youth Haven in Barrie. It was a chance to combine something we wanted to experience together with support for people in our community.</p><PhotoCarousel photos={personalPhotos} id="personal-photos" label="Trips and hobbies" cycling/></section>
  </div>
</Layout>
